<HelpTab>
    <HelpSection Title="Update rings">
        <FluentText>On a kiosk's <strong>Updates</strong> tab, choose <strong>Which version this PC runs</strong>:</FluentText>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Stable</strong> (recommended): the release approved for every PC.</li>
            <li><strong>Canary</strong>: tries each new release on this PC first. Use one or two kiosks for this.</li>
            <li><strong>Pinned</strong>: stays on one <strong>Version</strong> until you change it.</li>
        </ul>
        <FluentText>
            The tab shows what the PC is running and what it should be on. A change applies the next time the
            client restarts, or straight away with <strong>Update now</strong>.
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>

    <HelpSection Title="Kiosk Releases (Lanyard staff only)">
        <FluentText>
            <a href="/manage/client-releases">Kiosk Releases</a> is for Lanyard's own platform admins. New kiosk
            software goes to Canary PCs first. When it has run well there, <strong>Promote</strong> it so every
            Stable PC gets it. If a release causes problems, <strong>Withdraw</strong> it and PCs move back to the one
            before. <strong>Restore</strong> undoes a withdrawal. These changes affect every company.
        </FluentText>
    </HelpSection>
</HelpTab>
